    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0ba0ede5-480d-55fc-9235-01f8261c25f2",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7e01e701-0059-51a9-91ba-a1ac7a2e2db4",
